{"blocks":[["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-1356","Spoken Words from Person/codekiln",["Chapters","00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","00:00 Launchpad playing infini pad"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-1423","00:00 — Preset 259 Infini Pad.",["00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","00:00 Launchpad playing infini pad","Spoken Words from Person/codekiln"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-1463","03:07 Envelopes, Fold and Noise",["Infini Pad bass and 8bitfi","Chapters","00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-1505","Notes from",["Chapters","00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","03:07 Envelopes, Fold and Noise"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-1539","The main envelope's Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03 Bottom/05 Envelope/Knob/Attack, Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03 Bottom/05 Envelope/Knob/Decay Rel, Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03 Bottom/05 Envelope/Knob/Sustain and Microfreak/UI/Front/Row/03 Bottom/05 Envelope/Knob/Filter Amt are reshaped, followed by the cycling envelope's Fall, Rise and Hold.",["00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","03:07 Envelopes, Fold and Noise","Notes from"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-1898","Fold and Noise sweep through the pad; a third layer enters at 04:47.",["00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","03:07 Envelopes, Fold and Noise","Notes from"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-1974","Microfreak/UG/09 Envelope Gen/03 Envelope Stages · Microfreak/UG/06 Dig Osc/03 Types/14 BASS",["00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","03:07 Envelopes, Fold and Noise","Notes from"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-2083","05:12 Infini Pad as bass",["Infini Pad bass and 8bitfi","Chapters","00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-2118","My Notes",["Chapters","00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","05:12 Infini Pad as bass"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-2137","05:15 - the bass comes in - Infini Pad works great as a bass if the Microfreak/UI/Oscillator/Knob/Shape is turned up so the noise comes through.",["00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","05:12 Infini Pad as bass","My Notes"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-2293","07:05 - The minor seventh is a great bass interval.",["00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","05:12 Infini Pad as bass","My Notes"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-2352","Notes from",["Chapters","00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","05:12 Infini Pad as bass"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-2386","Infini Pad comes down to earth: the MicroFreak keys sound G1 and the F1 below it. The Launchpad leaves its G3 to B♭5 range and carries the bass line on from 05:56 through G1, F1, D2 and B♭1, down to D1 at 07:16. Saturate and Fold move through the bass.",["00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","05:12 Infini Pad as bass","Notes from"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-2650","Music/Concept/Scientific Pitch Notation",["00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad","05:12 Infini Pad as bass","Notes from"]],["GitP/A/Session/26/11/01-Sun/","source-block-2701","07:30 Filter-envelope sweeps",["Infini Pad bass and 8bitfi","Chapters","00:00 Enter Microfreak/Preset/259 Infini Pad"]]],"format_version":5}